# Packages the NixOS package repository holds (hps-starter sync nixos).
# One per line: NAME [OUTPUT]. NAME is the nixpkgs package name without its
# version; the release's own store-paths list says which store path that is
# (the one whose closure holds the starter's glibc, that is x86_64). With no
# OUTPUT the default output is meant, else the named one. A name that the
# release holds in several versions (openssl) is refused as ambiguous, so it
# is not listed: step 2 decides how the agent gets openssl.
# The repository holds each package's whole closure. ZFS is in the stock
# starter and is not listed.
libvirt
qemu-host-cpu-only
open-iscsi
mdadm
targetcli-fb
perl
# Perl modules the ctrl-exec agent uses (a perl module is listed by its
# name without the perl5.NN.N- prefix). A pure-Perl module (JSON) has no glibc
# in its closure, so its x86_64 copy cannot be told from the others by that
# test: it is not listed. Step 2 settles how the agent gets JSON.
IO-Socket-SSL
Net-SSLeay
